-- Seed: coverage rules from the OH and NC Medicaid fee schedules.
--
-- These answer the ONE attribute the policy documents could not: is the
-- code payable at all. A fee schedule is the authority — a code carrying
-- a payment amount is covered; a code marked discontinued is not.
--
-- Read DETERMINISTICALLY from the published spreadsheets (SheetJS over
-- the .xlsx cells). No LLM, so no hallucination surface: source_quote is
-- the row as published.
--
-- Ohio status codes, per the legend on the MSRIAP tab:
--   1 = initial maximum payment amount
--   2 = change in maximum payment amount as of the effective date
--   3 = discontinued coverage
-- Ohio also states that G0001-G9999 are not covered unless otherwise
-- indicated, which makes G0179/G0180 a citable not-covered rather than
-- merely absent.
--
-- FAN-OUT AND ITS LIMIT
-- A state fee schedule is the state's coverage determination, and under
-- Medicaid managed care a plan must cover what the state covers — so it
-- fans out to that state's MEDICAID plans. It does NOT fan out to
-- commercial plans: Ohio Medicaid has no authority over Anthem BCBS Ohio
-- commercial or Humana Ohio commercial, and asserting coverage for them
-- would be invention. Those two therefore gain nothing here.
--
-- The rate stored is the state FEE-FOR-SERVICE maximum. A plan's
-- contracted rate may differ, and the answer text says so rather than
-- implying the plan pays this amount. confidence 0.85 reflects that the
-- coverage determination is the state's, applied to the plan.
--
-- WITHHELD: NC 99343. Ohio marks it discontinued from 01/01/2023 (the
-- CPT boundary at which the home-visit family was restructured) while NC
-- still prices it with an open end date. Neither document states the code
-- was deleted, so asserting either way would exceed the sources. Ohio's
-- not_covered ships because it prevents a bad claim; NC's covered does
-- not, because it would invite one. Confirm against the current CPT book
-- before billing it.
--
-- 113 rules across 9 payer/state pairs.
-- Idempotent: deterministic UUIDs + ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE.

